answer/id #uuid "e145844b-7979-5eb0-a240-56b9f9f42d4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580741} {:answer/id #uuid "e94091f4-18d7-5f6c-9b7f-e55c81c8c49a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580754} {:answer/id #uuid "ef19b835-2f51-52cc-a2f9-fc1904cea930" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580766}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e94091f4-18d7-5f6c-9b7f-e55c81c8c49a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580754} :answer-field/id #uuid "d4c9d1da-6b89-5ab2-8c06-0bef819742ce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580868}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "95cc69d7-bf4f-55ce-b10c-871c735fbc08" :question/math-academy-id "q-65178" :question/problem "If $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3},$ then $\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-2\\pi )-2=$" :question/worked-solution "The period of $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ is $2\\pi .$ Therefore, for an integer $n$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+2n\\pi ).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=-1$ into the right-hand-side gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x &=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-2\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3},$ then $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-2\\pi )=\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3}.$\n\nFinally, then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-2\\pi )-2 & =\\sqrt{5}(\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3})-2 \\\\  & =\\frac{{(\\sqrt{5})}^{2}}{3}-2 \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}-2 \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} 